#2100
The credit room~
   I stuck my nose in again. This time on a challenge from
Vex, and because of numerous complaints from players about
what a waste of space this area was.
   I found a small Celtic fable and tried to make the area 
into it. The story is of the Saving of Tara. The story is
also at the incoming ftp, if you would like to read.
   I also tried something new, I placed clipart into a mobs
description. And it worked, to me looks kewl. And credit
for art goes to Goodwin, I stole off the web.
   The level of play here is 25+, due to the eq and objects
that can be gotten. Plus is more for rouge classes, th, sd,
and as. That was more on accident. The eq just seem to fit
them more, and the sleeping mobs seemed like they would be
quite inviting to any of that class with a smidgen of
brains. I put no +hp, +dam, +mana or +anything. I used con,
dex ect, and never more than 1 per item. 
   Anyway, enough rambling, hope it's up to par, and worth
the bandwidth.
Hasana
